  "rationale": "Budget and round cap are both exhausted (400/400 evals, round 4 of 4), so no further exploration is possible. The run is not infeasible: 107 of 400 evaluations are feasible (87 unique) and the feasible Pareto front holds 22 designs, so all three constraints are simultaneously satisfiable — throughput_msps best seen 190 (>= 32), max_abs_err best seen 5.42e-08 (<= 2.44e-04), sys_p99_batch_us best seen 0.2 us (<= 0.5 us). The front is well covered on both objectives: area_um2 spans 40611..81649 against the HV reference 100000, and accuracy_bits spans 12.5..18.7 against the HV reference 12, with hypervolume still improving (+8.2% this round) rather than plateauing. All four registry families were explored; only pipelined produced feasible designs (iterative 0/5, unrolled_k 0/15, pipelined_m 0/175 feasible), which is consistent with the 32 requests/us burst requirement favouring a 1-result/cycle architecture. The selection rule (min area_um2) picks the pipelined data_width=18 n_iter=14 angle_guard=3 frac_guard=0 rounding=round design at area_um2=40611, accuracy_bits=12.5, max_abs_err=1.7e-04 (2^-12.53), throughput_msps=128 — it meets the error bound with margin and its 128 MSPS throughput is 4x the 32 MSPS requirement, giving headroom for the L2 system simulation to confirm the 0.5 us p99 batch bound. Stopping here leaves the best mapped front for the spec's selection rule."
